## 1. Deny-by-default (pass, apart from F1)
- claude-code.ts: TOOLS "Read,Grep,Glob,Bash"; ALLOWED_TOOLS = Read, Grep, Glob and the 7 Bash rules
  (bare, context, context *, query, query *, check, check *). WebFetch and providers are gone. One
  module constant POLICY_FLAGS is spread into both start and resume: --restricted
  --strict-mcp-config --permission-mode dontAsk --tools --allowedTools.
- Only claude spawn site in packages/apps/adapters/scripts: claude-code.ts:105 (plus :142, --version).
- Matcher: Bash(P) exact, Bash(P *) prefix+space. A non-Bash(...) shape, a ':' or a '*' elsewhere
  admits everything. Conservative as briefed.
- Verb universe: regex over USAGE lines plus zz-future-verb, and a guard asserts run/red/greenlight/
  answer/budget/talk/tick/providers. Cross-checked against main.ts dispatch: every dispatched verb
  appears in USAGE, and the verb is always argv[0].

